        "date": "2026-11-13T06:18:08Z"
      },
      "message": "test(thread): pin the pass-control stamp, the negative-finish refusal and the M4 reset\n\nM3's review of PR #1219 asked for three pins:\n\n- `operation::tests_thread_stamp::thread_stamp_follows_every_pass_control`:\n  each of schedule, finish, spring, allowance, spindle_reverse and\n  cutter_left moves the stamp (measured against a base with every field\n  off its default, so the 0xE8 tag alone cannot hide a dropped field),\n  and the default pass control leaves the pre-#988 digest.\n- The negative-finish refusal is now a case in the kernel test\n  (`a_cutter_hand_against_the_spindle_and_other_nonsense_are_refused_by_name`)\n  and the door test (`impossible_pass_control_is_refused_when_the_operation_is_made`).\n- `an_m3_thread_after_an_m4_thread_posts_m3_again` pins the Fanuc\n  `spinRev` reset on OperationName.\n\nAlso gives `stamp_follows_every_input`'s #985 Thread fixture the new\n`passes` field after merging #1137's head.\n\nRefs #988\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
